WEBVTT

00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:07.750
Tomorrow,
we are going to find the explorer.

00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:09.625
Love from Paddington.

00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:10.792
Oh.

00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:13.708
PS. That is now my name.

00:00:50.875 --> 00:00:52.417
Good evening, Grant.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.375
Madam Director.

00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.042
Another delivery from the docks?

00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:03.458
Bring it through.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.083
Yes!

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:27.792
You are going to make
a fantastic addition to the collection.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.250
Aren't you worried
people will ask questions?

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:34.958
Not at all. As far as the tree-huggers
who run this place are concerned,

00:01:35.042 --> 00:01:37.875
I'd never dream of stuffing
a poor defenceless animal.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:43.208
However, it's not enough for me just
to look after this dusty old collection.

00:01:43.292 --> 00:01:46.500
I need to add the odd choice specimen
of my own.

00:01:47.292 --> 00:01:49.833
There was some weird sort of animal
at the dock today.

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.333
Oh, yes?

00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:54.500
Yeah.
I was doing my rounds as usual

00:01:54.625 --> 00:01:57.458
when I spotted something sticky
on the deck of the boat.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.458
I think they were paw prints.

00:02:00.708 --> 00:02:02.250
Whatever it was that had made them

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:04.417
had hidden himself away
in the lifeboat.

00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:08.708
Must have been in there
all the way from Peru.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.875
Seems to have lived
on nothing but marmalade.

00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:14.292
Did you say marmalade?

00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:16.583
- Hmm.
- What happened to him?

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.708
- He sneaked out in the mail van.
- Yes?

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.625
- I tracked him to Paddington.
- Good.

00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:21.958
But then he disappeared.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.250
I'm sorry. It's just that that creature
means a great deal to me.

00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:28.625
Why? Is he endangered?

00:02:31.542 --> 00:02:32.750
He is now.

00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:53.083
Oof!

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.792
Now, I know you all like marmalade,
but this is my sandwich.

00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:09.375
Erm, you're not using those ear brushes
to clean your mouth, are you, Mr Brown?

00:03:10.375 --> 00:03:12.167
Peculiar habit.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.375
Morning!

00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:18.583
Awesome.

00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:20.875
Jonathan.
Don't even think about it.

00:03:20.958 --> 00:03:23.792
34 per cent of pre-breakfast accidents
involve banisters.

00:03:23.875 --> 00:03:26.500
- But Paddington...
- I don't care what Paddington...

00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:40.125
-  Whoa.

00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:45.375
- It's so annoying, Mum.
- What is, pumpkin?

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.042
All my bathroom stuff is mined.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:50.333
Well, I've never liked you
using harsh chemicals, darling.

00:03:50.417 --> 00:03:52.417
They play havoc on people's skin.

00:03:53.458 --> 00:03:55.583
- Morning, Judy.
- Hello.

00:03:56.292 --> 00:03:59.625
- Why is Dad so boring and annoying?
- It's for your own good.

00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:01.083
Be nice, darlings.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:02.958
All I was trying to do was wash my face.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.333
Oh.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.000
Better?

00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:14.125
Come on, you two,
or you'll be late for school.

00:04:16.958 --> 00:04:20.292
Heck of a racket
coming from your way last night, Brown.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:22.917
Hello, Mr Curry.
I'm sorry if we disturbed you.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:23.917
Good morning.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.833
- I don't believe I've had the pleasure.
- Mr Curry, this is Paddington.

00:04:28.042 --> 00:04:30.083
- He's a bear.
- I can see that.

00:04:31.042 --> 00:04:34.167
- You must be a long way from home.
- I'm from Darkest Peru.

00:04:34.875 --> 00:04:37.333
- Oh.
- Don't worry, Mr Curry, he's going.

00:04:38.042 --> 00:04:42.667
Just as well. Don't want to be kept up
by any of your loud jungle music.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.333
Don't tell anyone at school
about Paddington.

00:04:48.417 --> 00:04:49.583
Why not?

00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:52.917
Because everyone thinks
we're weird enough without the bear.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.500
♪ Ba, ba, ba, ba

00:04:59.042 --> 00:04:59.917
♪ Ba, ba, ba, ba

00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:03.500
♪ Ba, ba, ba, ba...

00:05:04.792 --> 00:05:06.333
Hello there.

00:05:07.917 --> 00:05:09.667
Ooh! Dog!

00:05:11.292 --> 00:05:14.833
Where's that bear? Now, watch out.
There are thieves, murderers

00:05:14.875 --> 00:05:17.458
and pickpockets on every platform.
So follow us

00:05:17.542 --> 00:05:19.375
- and do exactly as you're told.
- Right-o.

